    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>An imperial city from 1218, Zürich was ruled by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guild">guilds</a> after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rudolf-brun">Rudolf Brun</a>’s revolution of 1336 and joined the Confederacy in 1351.</li><li>Its citizens governed a large rural territory through bailiffs, and the city led the Confederacy as its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vorort">Vorort</a>.</li><li>Under Zwingli and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heinrich-bullinger">Bullinger</a> it became a fountainhead of Reformed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestantism">Protestantism</a> with influence across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zurich-bible">Zürich Bible</a>, printed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christoph-froschauer">Christoph Froschauer</a>, was completed in 1531, three years before <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/martin-luther">Martin Luther</a>’s complete German Bible appeared.</p></aside>
    </section>

